# Make a copy of this file as `url.env` in the project root.

# These variables are read by `server.ts` (the Node/Express process), and by the
# Expo Metro bundler. Variables that start with "EXPO_PUBLIC_" are bundled into
# the client JS bundle and uploaded to the final application/device. Avoid
# passing server-side secrets here.

# Please note that this variable expects the "host", not a full URL. For
# example, you would drop the scheme from an ngrok URL.
# If ngrok returns "https://<SOME-EXAMPLE-DOMAIN>.ngrok.app", you would only
# put "<SOME-EXAMPLE-DOMAIN>.ngrok.app".
EXPO_PUBLIC_REFERENCE_COMPONENTS_DEV_SERVER_HOST=<SOME-EXAMPLE-DOMAIN>.ngrok.app
